/-!
# Safety certificate chained replay

The chunk theorems of each obligation chained through `safetyStepFast_chain`
into the fast replay of the whole section, its conversion to a run of the
trusted checker `safetyStep` by `safetyStepFast_sound`, and the three final
theorems: unit independence of the carrier and base unions and cross-safety of
the micro-representative and plug unions. The conversion is one-directional:
an accepted fast replay yields an accepted trusted run, and nothing is claimed
about the converse. The four role tables are exact assets of the 42-term
construction under
`data/k42/`.
The certificate is the documented output of `export_certificate.py` over those
tables; it is identified here by its SHA-256 and is not retained in the
repository, since the generated `Data/` modules carry every replayed record.
